# Secrets Manager: **${instance_name}**

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Portal** | [Open in STACKIT Portal](${instance_url}) |
| **API URL** | ${api_url} |
| **KV Mount** | `${kv_mount}` |

Project members with a Secrets Manager role log in with their STACKIT access token:

```sh
export VAULT_ADDR=${api_url}
export VAULT_TOKEN=$(stackit auth get-access-token)
vault kv list -mount=${kv_mount} /
```

Workloads use a user you [create](${users_url}) for this instance in the STACKIT portal:

```sh
export VAULT_ADDR=${api_url}
vault login -method=userpass username=<username>
vault kv put -mount=${kv_mount} my-app/db password=...
vault kv get -mount=${kv_mount} my-app/db
```
%{ if length(unknown_users) > 0 ~}

### ⚠️ Users Not Found

STACKIT does not know these users, so they did not get their Secrets Manager roles:

%{ for email in unknown_users ~}
- `${email}`
%{ endfor ~}

**To resolve this**, each user must sign in to the [STACKIT Portal](https://portal.stackit.cloud)
at least once. After they have signed in, re-run this building block and they will get their roles.
%{ endif ~}
%{ if length(covered_roles) > 0 ~}

### Roles Skipped

These users already hold project roles that include all permissions of the role, so it was not granted again:

%{ for covered in covered_roles ~}
- `${covered.email}`: `${covered.role}`
